agriculture, industry, and others. Examples of bioﬂocculants
include alginate, cellulosic materials, starch, chitosan, xanthan
gum, Moringa oleifera, okra, guar gum and Cassia tora gum, and
tannins, which represent economically viable and safe
substitutes of synthetic ﬂocculants.14,15
