Pollutants Removal from Wastewater Samples. Chitin
(source of chitosan) and BSF can be obtained as byproducts
derived from industrial operations in Sinaloa, and eventually
these materials could be used for water remediation in this
state and other regions. Thus, ﬂocculation trials were
performed for water samples having the following average
values of some parameters: CCM: turbidity ≈ 160 NTU, pH ≈
6.33, total dissolved solids (TDS) ≈ 1175 mg L−1; La Escalera
(LE): turbidity ≈ 50 NTU, pH ≈ 7.48, TDS ≈ 292 mg L−1;
and ES: turbidity ≈ 22 NTU, pH ≈ 7.63, TDS ≈ 1015 mg L−1.
Evidently, high values of some parameters are a consequence
of alarming levels of diﬀerent contaminants. The ﬁrst test
consisted of analyzing the turbidity evolution at diﬀerent
ﬂocculant dosages (Figure 4). The eﬀectiveness in removing

